    "title": "How Does Lehigh University Rank Among America's Best Colleges?",
    "text": "Lehigh University is a private institution that was founded in 1865. In the 2026 edition of Best Colleges, Lehigh University is ranked No. #46 in National Universities. It's also ranked No. #24 in Best Value Schools. It has a total undergraduate enrollment of 5,911 (fall 2024), its setting is city, and the campus size is 2,355 acres. The student-faculty ratio at Lehigh University is 10:1, and it utilizes a semester-based academic calendar. Lehigh University accepts the Common Application and has a test-optional admissions policy. The school's tuition and fees are $67,920. Forty-four percent of first-year students receive need-based financial aid, and the average net price for federal loan recipients is $32,125. The four-year graduation rate is 80%. Six years after graduation, the median salary for graduates is $88,810.Lehigh University is a private institution that was founded in 1865. In the 2026 edition of Best Colleges, Lehigh University is ranked No. #46 in National Universities. It's also ranked No. #24 in Best Value Schools. It has a total undergraduate enrollment of 5,911 (fall 2024), its setting is city, and the campus size is 2,355 acres. The student-faculty ratio at Lehigh University is 10:1, and it utilizes a semester-based academic calendar. Lehigh University accepts the Common Application and has a test-optional admissions policy. The school's tuition and fees are $67,920. Forty-four percent of first-year students receive need-based financial aid, and the average net price for federal loan recipients is $32,125. The four-year graduation rate is 80%. Six years after graduation, the median salary for graduates is $88,810.",
